  "scenario": "A remote worker has moved into a thin-walled apartment and spends most of the day on calls. Their clicky mechanical keyboard is disruptive, but they do not want a soft or unreliable typing feel. They are considering the 122.99-dollar Mistel X-VIII Cherry MX Silent Red variant, have seen O-rings suggested for the current board, and want to know whether either path is actually shown to reach the quietness of a membrane-style keyboard at the call microphone or across the wall. The available material contains the exact Mistel offer, one direct experience with a different dampened silent switch, one direct experience with a different under-stem damping modification, and independent references for source-to-observer quieting, acoustic measurement, and airborne wall attenuation. It contains no direct O-ring outcome, no independent Mistel acoustic test, and no matched membrane, call-microphone, or through-wall comparison.",
  "constraints": [
    "treat_the_mistel_price_rating_variant_and_acoustic_language_as_a_frozen_seller_observation_not_an_independent_noise_test",
